"rules": [
 "A subcategory exists only where the work, and so the skills, meaningfully differ — that is what lets Atlas reuse it as a role node with its own skill set.",
 "Every category has a 'general' subcategory: category clear, specialisation unsure → shown at category level, never held (D127's hold applies to the category only).",
 "Level is a facet, not a subcategory: intern · junior · mid · senior · staff · principal · manager · director · executive. People-management roles sit in their function's category at a manager / director level (an engineering manager is Software engineering · Manager).",
 "Industry is a company facet (from the company page), not a job category: 'Backend at a fintech' = Software engineering › Backend + the company's industry.",
 "Classification reads the posting's content, not only its title; aliases are hints for title normalisation.",
 "soc = 2018 US SOC codes (D127 compatibility). family = the Atlas family the subcategory belongs to; 'NEW: …' marks a family Atlas doesn't have yet.",
 "Ids are stable: a rename keeps its id; a split or merge is a new version with a mapping from old ids."
],
